## §6 Where I think the reviewer is wrong (not applied)
1. ur-a row 1 (P1). The reviewer reads the Urdu as "reversing the English source". It does diverge from the English —
   on purpose. RULEBOOK-FIX R3 rewrote exactly these three sentences in every locale because a sentence telling a reader
   that courts "generally impose about 3 months" reads as a predicted outcome under the Taiwan attorney advertising rules.
   Restoring the English degree would undo a supervisor rule and an ACCEPTED-ROUND skip rule at once. Decision for the
   supervisor, not for this lane. (Same reasoning applies to the identical sentences in ko/en/ja/zh-hant, which
   RULEBOOK-FIX already lists as an open user decision.)
2. ur-a row 34. The reviewer wants "زیادہ سے زیادہ معاوضہ" ("the maximum compensation available") restored because the
   English says so. R3 explicitly replaces "pursue the maximum / highest possible compensation" with "pursue the
   compensation the facts and evidence support". I applied only the grammatical half of the row — "اس کے پیچھے لگے" was
   indeed not Urdu — and the sentence now reads "… اور حقائق و ثبوت سے جو معاوضہ ثابت ہو، اس کے حصول کے لیے کوشش کرے۔"
   The superlative is deliberately not restored.
3. ur-a row 15. The reviewer asks for the redundant gloss "(3 میں سے 1)" / "(3 میں سے 2)" to be deleted outright. Deleting
   it removes the digits the checker counts against the Korean source: measured on a temp copy, that is
   `numbers FAIL missing from translation` in 001, 002 (×8), 005, 016 and 018 — summary FAIL 13/18. I applied the row in
   the form that fixes the machine feel and keeps the digits: "ایک تہائی (1/3)" / "دو تہائی (2/3)", 13 instances
   (001×2, 002×9, 005×1, 016×2, 018×1). Verified: summary PASS 18/18.
4. ur-b row 6 — see §5. The characters are in the source, and the gate pins them.
5. Not an error, but a note for the next round: the ur-b verdict calls the U+200B lines "reported in r4 and still on disk".
   They will stay on disk for as long as the Korean source has them; re-listing them each round costs the lane a P2 slot.

